<template>
    <div class="page">

        <div class="navbar">
            <div class="navbar-bg"></div>
            <div class="navbar-inner">
                <div class="left">
                    <a href="#" class="link back">
                        <i class="icon icon-back"></i>
                        <span class="ios-only">Back</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div class="title">Protocol handling</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="page-content">

            <div class="block-title block-title-large">Protocol handling</div>
            <div class="block">
                <p>
                    Protocol handling enables web apps to register their ability to open links with particular URL schemes, also known as protocols. <br/>
                    This means that a web app can for example register itself as an app that will open links like web+foo://bar.
                    In this case, the app will register the protocol web+foo as the protocol it can handle. <br/>
                    If a user chooses the web app as the default app to open links with this protocol, the web app will be opened when a link with this protocol is clicked.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><twig:Link href="web+symphone://geolocation">Geolocation (web+symphone://geolocation)</twig:Link></li>
                    <li><twig:Link href="web+symphone://screen-capturing">Screen Capturing (web+symphone://screen-capturing)</twig:Link></li>
                </ul>
                {% set yaml = 'pwa:
    manifest:
        enabled: true
        protocol_handlers:
            - protocol: "web+symphone"
              placeholder: "type"
              url:
                  path: "app_protocol_handler"
' %}
                <pre><code class="language-yaml" data-controller="code">{{ yaml|raw }}</code></pre>
                <p>
                    This will register the protocol web+symphone as the protocol it can handle.
                    The final URL will be <code>https://example.com/path/?type=%s</code>.<br/>
                    The placeholder %s will be replaced by the value of the link (e.g. <code>web+symphone://geolocation</code> or <code>web+symphone://screen-capturing</code>).
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>
</template>

